# Copy this file to .env and fill in your keys. .env is git-ignored.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key-here

# Optional overrides — uncomment to change defaults.
# GRIFFIN_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# GRIFFIN_NAME=Griffin

# Tier 3 — voice
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=your-deepgram-api-key-here
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key-here
# Defaults to ElevenLabs' premade "Rachel" voice until you pick one.
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=21m00Tcm4TlvDq8ikWAM
# Which key to hold to talk: ctrl_r, ctrl_l, alt_r, alt_l, or space.
# GRIFFIN_PTT_KEY=ctrl_r

# Tier 10 — Discord bridge (griffin/discord_bridge.py, discord_main.py).
# Chat with Griffin from Discord (phone or desktop) instead of only a
# local terminal. Not needed for main.py/voice_main.py/heartbeat_main.py.
#
# 1. Go to https://discord.com/developers/applications -> New Application
#    (name it anything, e.g. "Griffin").
# 2. Bot tab -> Reset Token -> copy it -> that's DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN.
# 3. Same Bot tab -> turn ON "Message Content Intent" (under Privileged
#    Gateway Intents) — the bridge can't read your messages without this.
# 4. OAuth2 -> URL Generator -> scope "bot" -> permissions "Send Messages"
#    and "Read Message History" -> open the generated URL -> invite the
#    bot to a server (create a small private one just for this if you
#    don't have one — you need to share a server with the bot once to be
#    able to DM it directly afterward).
# 5. In Discord, enable Developer Mode (User Settings -> Advanced), then
#    right-click your own name/profile -> Copy User ID -> that's
#    DISCORD_OWNER_ID. This is the ONLY id the bridge will ever respond
#    to — everyone else, and every non-DM message, is silently ignored.
# 6. DM the bot directly (find it in the server you invited it to) once
#    it's running.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=your-discord-bot-token-here
DISCORD_OWNER_ID=your-discord-user-id-here

# Tier 7 — optional: proxy model calls through Helicone (helicone.ai) so
# Griffin's and every specialist's activity shows up as a live trace in a
# web dashboard. Leave unset to talk to Anthropic directly, unchanged.
# HELICONE_API_KEY=your-helicone-api-key-here

# Tier 7 — youtube specialist's Reddit story sourcing. Recommended: Reddit
# increasingly 403s unauthenticated requests to its JSON endpoints, so
# without these, story fetching is unreliable. Get a free "script" app at
# https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps ("create app" -> type: script; the
# redirect URI field is required but unused for this, put anything like
# http://localhost). No Reddit login/password is used at runtime — just
# the client ID (under the app name) and secret it gives you.
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=your-reddit-app-client-id-here
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=your-reddit-app-client-secret-here

# Tier 9 — send_email (griffin/tools/send.py), via Resend's HTTPS API.
# This tool always requires your explicit yes before it runs (config.yaml's
# requires_confirmation), same as any other "sends a message" action.
#
# Originally this used plain SMTP with whatever provider you already had
# (Gmail, iCloud, Outlook) — dropped after a live deploy proved cloud
# platforms commonly block outbound SMTP entirely as an anti-spam policy
# (confirmed: both Gmail's and iCloud's mail servers were unreachable from
# Railway, while HTTPS calls worked fine). Resend is HTTPS-based, so it
# works the same locally or on Railway.
#
# 1. Sign up at https://resend.com — free tier, no credit card needed to start.
# 2. Dashboard -> API Keys -> Create API Key -> copy it.
# 3. Without a verified domain (the default), Resend only lets you send
#    FROM their placeholder address (onboarding@resend.dev) TO the exact
#    email address your Resend account is signed up with — their
#    anti-spam restriction for unverified senders, not a bug here. Fine
#    for testing; to send to other recipients or from your own address,
#    verify a domain you own under Domains in their dashboard (needs
#    access to that domain's DNS settings) — optional, skip it for now
#    if testing is enough.
RESEND_API_KEY=your-resend-api-key-here
# Only change this once you've verified your own domain with Resend.
# RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=onboarding@resend.dev

# Tier 11 — publisher (griffin/agents/publisher.py, griffin/youtube/upload.py):
# uploads an already-produced video (youtube_produce) to YouTube via the
# YouTube Data API v3. Also always requires your explicit yes before it
# runs, and defaults to a private upload on top of that.
#
# A plain API key can't authorize uploading to a channel — YouTube needs
# OAuth2 user consent. Setup:
# 1. https://console.cloud.google.com -> create a project (or use an
#    existing one) -> APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data
#    API v3".
# 2. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen -> External -> fill in the
#    minimum (app name, your email) -> add your own Google account under
#    "Test users" (leaving the app in "Testing" status is fine for
#    personal use — see the note below on what that costs you).
# 3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client
#    ID -> Application type "Desktop app" -> that gives you
#    YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID and YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET below.
# 4. Set those two in .env, then run `python3 youtube_auth.py` once, from
#    your own machine (it opens a browser for you to sign in and consent)
#    — it prints YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN for you to paste in below.
#
# Note: while the OAuth consent screen is in "Testing" status (the
# default, and the simplest setup for personal use), the refresh token
# youtube_auth.py mints expires after 7 days — re-run it to get a new one
# when that happens. Submitting the app for Google's verification removes
# that limit but is real extra process not covered here.
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id-here
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-oauth-client-secret-here
YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN=from-running-youtube_auth.py
